{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "GWDOParameters",
    "description": "Scheme constants of WRF's orographic gravity-wave drag and low-level flow-blocking scheme (GWDO, `gwd_opt = 1`), transcribed one-for-one from the `real(kind=kind_phys), parameter` and `integer, parameter` declarations of `phys/physics_mmm/bl_gwdo.F90` (WRF 4.8, NCAR/MMM-physics CCPP kernel `bl_gwdo_run`; the Hong et al. 2025 revision of Choi and Hong 2015). Mounted by every GWDO component as subsystem `par` so that no tuning constant is written inline in the physics. Every constant is declared `real(kind=kind_phys), parameter` but INITIALISED FROM A DEFAULT-REAL LITERAL, so in a real64 build the scheme runs the binary64 widening of the literal's binary32 value -- the same defect N2 records for YSU and WSM6 and N45/N101 for the KPP mechanisms. Fifteen of the twenty-one literals are exactly representable in binary32 and are unaffected (0.25, 1., -100., 0., 10., 1., 10., 1., 10., 50., 1., 10., 10., 0., 750.). SIX ARE NOT, and the values below are their widened binary32 roundings, not their decimals: `ce` = 0.800000011920929, `bnv2min` and `olmin` = 9.999999747378752e-06, `odmin` = 0.10000000149011612, `pcutoff_den` = 0.009999999776482582, `qmin` = 1.0000000031710769e-30 (FORTRAN_BUGS N103). Only `ce` reaches an answer on the reference set -- it is the exponent of the asymmetry enhancement (oa + 2)^(ce Fr), where its 1.5e-8 relative offset becomes 1.5e-9 to 4.6e-9 in efac and in the launch stress. Carrying the roundings makes the agreement EXACT; carrying the decimals misses the real64 kernel by that amount, which is above the rel 1e-9 contract. The SIX constants GWDO does NOT declare -- g, cp, R_d, R_v, eps_1 and pi -- arrive as subroutine arguments from WRF's real32 `module_model_constants`, and pi arrives as the truncated inline literal `3.141592653` of `module_pbl_driver.F:2192` rather than `piconst` (FORTRAN_BUGS N102); those come from `lib/wrf_constants.esm`, not from here.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["wrf", "gravity-wave-drag", "gwdo", "orography", "scheme-constants"],
    "references": [
      { "citation": "Hong, S.-Y., and co-authors (2025). Revision of the orographic gravity wave drag parameterization in the KIAPS Integrated Model. Wea. Forecasting." },
      { "citation": "Choi, H.-J., and S.-Y. Hong (2015). An updated subgrid orographic parameterization for global atmospheric forecast models. J. Geophys. Res. Atmos. 120, 12445-12457.", "doi": "10.1002/2015JD024230" },
      { "citation": "Kim, Y.-J., and A. Arakawa (1995). Improvement of orographic gravity wave parameterization using a mesoscale gravity wave model. J. Atmos. Sci. 52, 1875-1902.", "doi": "10.1175/1520-0469(1995)052<1875:IOOGWP>2.0.CO;2" },
      { "citation": "Shutts, G. (1985). Gravity-wave drag parametrization over complex terrain: the effect of critical-level absorption in directional wind-shear. Quart. J. Roy. Meteor. Soc. 121, 1005-1021." },
      { "citation": "NCAR/MMM-physics bl_gwdo.F90 at commit 52cfbd7 (WRF 4.8 phys/physics_mmm submodule)." }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "GWDOParameters": {
      "variables": {
        "ric": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.25, "description": "Critical Richardson number. It is BOTH the branch test `rim <= ric` that selects the wave-saturation hypothesis AND the zero of the saturation factor 2 sqrt(temc) - temc that the branch then evaluates (temc = 2 + 1/sqrt(Ri) is 4 exactly at Ri = 0.25), which is the cancellation recorded as FORTRAN_BUGS N85." },
        "velmin": { "type": "parameter", "units": "m/s", "default": 1.0, "description": "Minimum wind speed. Used three ways: as the floor on the squared shear `max(dw2, velmin)` in the Richardson number (where it is dimensionally a squared speed, not a speed -- see the note in `column_state.esm`), as the floor on the low-level speed `ulow`, and as the floor on a small POSITIVE projected speed `velco`." },
        "dw2min": { "type": "parameter", "units": "m^2/s^2", "default": 1.0, "description": "Floor on the SQUARED vertical wind difference in the layer Richardson number, `shr2 = max(dw2, dw2min) rdz^2`. The Fortran spells this floor `velmin` -- the same symbol it uses for a wind SPEED -- so the comparison is between a squared speed and a speed. The numeric value is 1 either way, so nothing changes; this entry exists so that the .esm carries the floor with the units of the quantity it floors, per the repository rule that a constant never borrows another quantity's dimension." },
        "rimin": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": -100.0, "description": "Floor on the layer Richardson number `usqj`." },
        "bnv2min": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1/s^2", "default": 9.999999747378752e-06, "description": "Floor on the squared Brunt-Vaisala frequency before its square root is taken in the wave-saturation profile." },
        "efacmin": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.0, "description": "Lower clamp on the asymmetry enhancement factor efac." },
        "efacmax": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 10.0, "description": "Upper clamp on the asymmetry enhancement factor efac." },
        "frc": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 1.0, "description": "Critical Froude number, the scale in the enhancement-factor exponent ce*Fr/frc." },
        "frmax": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 10.0, "description": "Upper clamp on the Froude number Fr = N |var| od / ulow." },
        "ce": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.800000011920929, "description": "Mesoscale-model tuning coefficient in the enhancement factor efac = (oa + 2)^(ce Fr / frc)." },
        "cg": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 1.0, "description": "Mesoscale-model tuning coefficient in the convexity factor gfac = Fr^2 oc / (Fr^2 oc + cg)." },
        "var_min": { "type": "parameter", "units": "m", "default": 10.0, "description": "Minimum sub-grid orographic standard deviation. DECLARED BUT NEVER READ in bl_gwdo.F90 (WRF 4.8): the standard-deviation gate is `var <= 0`, not `var < var_min`. Kept here so the transcription of the parameter block is complete and the dead constant is visible." },
        "hmt_min": { "type": "parameter", "units": "m", "default": 50.0, "description": "Minimum sub-grid orographic maximum height. `omax <= hmt_min` switches the whole scheme off in a column. Because WPS 4.3 writes no ELVMAX, omax is identically 0 there and this gate silently disables GWDO everywhere (FORTRAN_BUGS B17)." },
        "oc_min": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 1.0, "description": "Lower clamp on the orographic convexity oc1." },
        "oc_max": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 10.0, "description": "Upper clamp on the orographic convexity oc1." },
        "olmin": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 9.999999747378752e-06, "description": "Floor on the orographic length fractions ol and olp (which are fractional widths, hence dimensionless)." },
        "odmin": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.10000000149011612, "description": "Lower clamp on the horizontal orographic aspect ratio od = olp/ol." },
        "odmax": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 10.0, "description": "Upper clamp on the horizontal orographic aspect ratio od = olp/ol." },
        "cdmin": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.0, "description": "Minimum bulk drag coefficient. DECLARED BUT NEVER READ in bl_gwdo.F90 (WRF 4.8): the flow-blocking drag coefficient is clamped with the inline literal `max(2 - 1/od, 0.)` instead. Kept for completeness of the transcription." },
        "pcutoff": { "type": "parameter", "units": "Pa", "default": 750.0, "description": "Pressure above which (p <= pcutoff, i.e. 7.5 hPa and higher) the mesosphere density limiter is applied to the drag." },
        "pcutoff_den": { "type": "parameter", "units": "kg/m^3", "default": 0.009999999776482582, "description": "Reference density of the mesosphere limiter: the drag is reduced by min(rho/pcutoff_den, 1)." },
        "qmin": { "type": "parameter", "units": "m/s^2", "default": 1.0000000031710769e-30, "description": "Threshold on |taud| below which no limiter is applied at all. It is compared against a stress divergence, so it carries that quantity's units." },
        "kgwdmin": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 2.0, "description": "Lowest admissible wave-launch (reference) level, as a level index. `integer, parameter` in the Fortran; carried as a real here because esm variables are real-valued and every use is a comparison against a level index." },
        "mdir": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 8.0, "description": "Number of sectors of the wind rose used to pick the orographic statistics along the low-level wind." }
      },
      "equations": []
    }
  }
}
